{"name":"Ballerina Silk","hex":"#f0dee0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballerina","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ballet dancer \n A female ballet dancer.\nEllipsis of prima ballerina (“the star female ballet performer in the company”).","A female ballet dancer.\nEllipsis of prima ballerina (“the star female ballet performer in the company”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballerina"},{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballet dancer","blocks":[{"text":"A ballet dancer is a person who practices the art of classical ballet. Both women and men can practice ballet. They rely on years of extensive training and proper technique to become a part of a professional ballet company. Ballet dancers are at a high risk of injury due to the demanding technique of ballet dancing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Corsaire_-Le_Jardin_Anime_-Pierina_Legnani_-Olga_Preobrajenska_-1899.jpg/330px-Corsaire_-Le_Jardin_Anime_-Pierina_Legnani_-Olga_Preobrajenska_-1899.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballet_dancer","wikidata":"Q805221"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk","wikidata":"Q37681"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/500px-Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/1280px-Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/500px-Monochrome_Ballet_Feet_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Many ballet dancers end up with injured feet due to the size of the shoes or the use of their feet in choreography","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonochrome_Ballet_Feet_(Unsplash).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg/1280px-Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1843.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ballerina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABallet-Ballerina-1843.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/NWFusionPaquitaPas2.jpg/500px-NWFusionPaquitaPas2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.o